From 2a39eb59fbbfef2d987c0b25b47aefeaeb19e370 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:13:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Turrets: hit chance follows CCP's destiny formula

Player, NPC and sentry turret hit chance now match Ballpark::GetAccuracy()
from CCP's open-sourced Carbon destiny (github.com/carbonengine/destiny):

- angular velocity uses only the relative velocity across the line of
  sight, so moving straight towards or away from a target no longer
  spoils tracking
- the falloff term uses surface-to-surface range instead of centre to
  centre
- the signature ratio only scales the tracking term; EVEmu's own rule that
  cut damage by targetSig / sigRes when a gun could track but out-sized
  its target is gone
- a wrecking shot has to hit first (a low roll used to wreck on a miss)

One shared helper does the maths for all three; drones already used the
same formula and are unchanged.
---
 .../ship/modules/TurretFormulas.cpp           | 219 ++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 96 insertions(+), 123 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/eve-server/ship/modules/TurretFormulas.cpp b/src/eve-server/ship/modules/TurretFormulas.cpp
index 0690e25..40d536c 100644
